# Block Drop — frontend

- Stay vanilla: no React/Vue, no npm, no bundler, no TypeScript transpile step.
- Share one global namespace: `window.BlockDrop`. New modules attach to it; do not invent a second global.
- Keep script concerns split (data / rules / UI loop / audio / high scores / touch). Prefer extending existing files over new frameworks.
- Load classic `<script>` tags in dependency order from `index.html` (and imprint only what it needs). Keep `theme-boot.js` blocking in `<head>` (FOUC). Mark the game scripts `defer` so they fetch in parallel and still run in order — prefer that over concatenating (no bundler).
- Version JS/CSS with a shared `?v=` query on every reference in HTML; **bump `?v=` whenever JS or CSS content changes** (no bundler/hashes). Deploy gives those files long immutable `Cache-Control`.
- Board and next-piece preview stay on canvas; layout in `css/styles.css`.
- Support keyboard and on-screen touch controls; preserve Safari-friendly click/tap behavior (no double-fire on rotate; Pause/Restart on press).
- High scores: client talks to `/api/scores` on the same origin; do not assume a separate API hostname.
- After game asset changes, bump `?v=` if needed, then deploy syncs `block-drop/` and invalidates CloudFront / purges Cloudflare.
